/*
  PDFRender - JBIG2 generic region decoding.  See h/pdfjbig2.

  Two pieces.  The MQ coder is the same adaptive binary arithmetic
  coder JPEG 2000 uses, driven by a table of probability states.  The
  generic region procedure decodes one pixel at a time, choosing the
  coder's context from a fixed template of pixels above and to the
  left - all of them already decoded, which is what lets the decoder
  form the same context the encoder did without being told it.

